Requires a job at level 10 before a character can /yell, and tells the player how
many seconds of the /yell cooldown remain (src/map/packets/c2s/0x0b5_chat_std.cpp).

The [YELL]Cooldown char var now holds the time the cooldown ends instead of 1.
It still expires on its own, so the cooldown survives zoning and relogging.
The length is still map.YELL_COOLDOWN, and the zone check and broadcast are unchanged.

A yell-banned player is now told they are banned and how long the ban has left
(read from the [YELL]Banned expiry), instead of the generic "cannot be used in this area".
!yell ban without a day count (scripts/commands/yell.lua) now stores expiry 0, a ban with
no end; it used to store the current time, so the "indefinite" ban expired at once.
---
diff --git a/scripts/commands/yell.lua b/scripts/commands/yell.lua
index 1973e0b9ab..e994a9ae62 100644
--- a/scripts/commands/yell.lua
+++ b/scripts/commands/yell.lua
@@ -53,7 +53,13 @@ commandObj.onTrigger = function(player, value, target, days)
             days = 0
         end
 
-        targ:setCharVar('[YELL]Banned', 1, GetSystemTime() + utils.days(days))
+        -- An expiry of 0 never expires. GetSystemTime() + 0 would expire at once.
+        local expiry = 0
+        if days > 0 then
+            expiry = GetSystemTime() + utils.days(days)
+        end
+
+        targ:setCharVar('[YELL]Banned', 1, expiry)
         player:printToPlayer(string.format('%s has been banned from using the /yell command.', targ:getName()))
     end
 end
